## Upstream artwork reused in this port

The logic-gate, Select, wiring and Pin glyphs in the toolbar and component explorer are
logisim-evolution's own icon drawings, transcribed from the 4.1.0 release as vector geometry
(`AbstractGate.paintIconANSI` and `paintIconBufferAnsi`, and the matching painters in
`gui.icons`, `tools` and `std.wiring`). They are upstream's artwork, reused under the same
licence, not this port's design.

The application's own mark and icon are **not** upstream's logo, which is their trade mark and
is not licensed to this port by the GPL — section 7(e) expressly contemplates trade-mark terms.
This build uses its own mark, name, bundle identifier and document type.

## Known divergences from upstream 4.1.0

Java component libraries (`.jar`), the vendor FPGA toolchains (Xilinx ISE and Vivado, Intel
Quartus) and the TCL console are not available in this build. Circuits that use them still
open, and their components are preserved exactly on save rather than being silently discarded.
